?oc=5","p":"Lawndale News","d":"2026-10-15T11:02:08Z","o":false,"dup":false},{"t":"Diplomatic Coercion: Chinese Sanctions On Belize And Paraguay","u":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihwFBVV95cUxQY2hBWERNc3BURkRIYUk1UVdMWWh3RENucEFBenZxeXF5Qmluczd0M1pQdEZlaVNiSDJZN09aRFFVQ2N0emJtZjNYX0wwdWRfQ0JXLWhSSTRtazJIbXZUZ0hXSk5tZG5tcXZTek5HNDdWaVFLRkRwVjZZb1B1OEFlVGJOc1pFVk0?oc=5","p":"The Organization for World Peace","d":"2026-10-16T17:27:44Z","o":false,"dup":false}],"related":[],"revisions":[],"entities":[{"name":"Taiwan","kind":"place","mentions":11},{"name":"China","kind":"place","mentions":10},{"name":"Belize","kind":"place","mentions":8},{"name":"Belizean","kind":"place","mentions":2},{"name":"Paraguayan","kind":"group","mentions":2},{"name":"Beijing","kind":"place","mentions":1},{"name":"Chinese Foreign Ministry","kind":"organisation","mentions":1},{"name":"Latin American","kind":"group","mentions":1}],"disputes":[],"summary":{"text":"China has imposed sanctions on Paraguayan and Belizean ministers over their support for Taiwan. This action is part of a broader diplomatic stance against countries that recognize Taiwan as part of China.","text_hi":null,"model":"qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:03:16Z"},"context":{"background":[{"title":"Cross-strait relations","extract":"Cross-strait relations are the political and economic relations between China and Taiwan across the Taiwan Strait. Due to the existing controversy over the status of Taiwan and the Chinese legitimacy question, they are also not defined as diplomatic relations by either side.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross-strait_relations","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"China","extract":"China, officially the People's Republic of China (PRC), is a country in East Asia. It is divided into 33 province-level divisions, including two special administrative regions. Beijing is the capital, while Shanghai is the most populous city by urban area. Its geography features the Central Plain, major rivers such as the Yangtze and Yellow River, deserts, subtropical and temperate forests, plateaus, and mountain ranges such as the Himalayas. It is the world's second-most populous country after India, with a population exceeding 1.4 billion. Covering 9.6 million square kilometers (3,700,000 sq mi), it is the third largest country by area.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"CN"},{"title":"Taiwan","extract":"Taiwan, officially the Republic of China (ROC), is a country in East Asia. The main island of Taiwan, formerly known as Formosa, lies between the East and South China Seas in the northwestern Pacific Ocean, with the People's Republic of China (PRC) to the northwest, Japan to the northeast, and the Philippines to the south. It has an area of 35,808 square kilometers, with mountain ranges dominating the eastern two-thirds and plains in the western third, where its highly urbanized population is concentrated. The combined territories under ROC control consist of 168 islands in total covering 36,193 square kilometers. The largest metropolitan area is formed by Taipei, New Taipei City, and Keelung. With around 23.9 million inhabitants, Taiwan is among the most densely populated countries.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"TW"}],"arc":{"reports":19,"first_seen":"2026-10-12T04:22:00Z","first_title":"China Sanctions Officials of Taiwan’s Partners for First Time","first_url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwgFBVV95cUxNZmtJamhVcURFeW9mTXJDWUVmeDJ6MHNGMlk5a0V1UXZuUmxqT2hxaVVTeXNvQ2dXSDdtZ2h3OGEzdEk5ZElObWc4b05UVnlXUmN6aC1XWWJyVWNjY3lVbHNWRVgzMUFRSkpSaE5COGN1NHJBOVlGQjlXR1dLcEJHMGVWWlJGUTlpZE1QbS0tUWlLUVcwN0F3R2lHNXloN0ZYWGdwWDR4VTA4RW1lcm1kSWNQekY5N2h4NGZZSGttZTRNZw?oc=5","first_publisher":"dailyrecordnews.com","earlier":[{"id":"e_edec9a6691dc","title":"China Sanctions Another Comp